{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"anti-shim|shim|canonical archive entry|degradation API test|artifact enrichment dependency|Related artifact version is unavailable|Producing process provenance is unavailable|source provenance is unavailable\\\" docs tests apps/platform -g '\"'!dist'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"tests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts:216:    ).toContain('Related artifact version is unavailable.');\ntests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts:320:      'Related artifact version is unavailable.',\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:46:## Orchestrator failure mode — Story 1 \"test-shim-as-scope-decision\" (2026-04-23 ~11:00Z)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:55:4. **Forgot the epic's own framing.** Epic 4 is a platform-integration standup. \"Tests pass against the in-memory shim\" is not equivalent to \"the platform integrates.\" Shape tests + shim tests without real substrate wiring produce a green gate that does not evidence the point of the epic.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:59:> A shim is only acceptable when there is a legit blocker — a design gap, a missing substrate, or a cross-story/cross-epic dependency that genuinely prevents integration. \"The production caller isn't wired yet\" is not a legit blocker when the read path can be seeded via a test. When the Convex substrate, contract, and tech-design guidance all exist, the integration must be wired — not shimmed — before acceptance.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:61:**Concrete orchestrator checks before disposing any \"test-shim-only\" finding as `accepted-risk`:**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:72:- Reason for reopen: on user review of Story 1's accepted-risk disposition, my rationale was wrong. The accepted \"test-shim only\" package path is a platform-integration gap, not an epic-scope decision. Specifically `ConvexPlatformStore.getProcessReviewPackage` is `return null` and `ConvexPlatformStore.listProcessReviewTargets` only enumerates artifacts, while `InMemoryPlatformStore` has the full package impl and tests pass against it. Tech design (tech-design-server.md §Module Responsibility Matrix) requires real Convex reads; the Convex substrate (`listPackageSnapshotsForProcess`, `getPackageSnapshot`, `listPackageSnapshotMembers`) already exists from Story 0. Self-review's \"spec deviation\" declaration and both verifiers' `blocking: true` finding were correct signals that the orchestrator should not have overridden on epic-scope grounds.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:129:Mock/shim audit findings from both verifiers (markdown-renderer scaffold, markdown-it-anchor/markdown-task-lists no-op, packages/markdown-package `NOT_IMPLEMENTED` throws, github-slugger lightweight stand-in): **not treated as findings** — these are expected Story 0 scaffold behavior. Later chunks (Stories 3 and 5) replace them. Both verifiers classified them as observations rather than blocking findings.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:392:- Reopen note: original acceptance (receipt below) accepted \"test-shim only\" package path as epic-scope decision; see **Orchestrator failure mode** section at top of log. Reopened on user review at 11:00Z; two bounded `story-continue` follow-ups wired the real Convex read path, then added unsupported-fallback reviewability and cross-kind newest-first target ordering.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:399:  - Round 1: `artifacts/01-.../007-verify-batch.json` (against initial impl; revise — shim finding that drove reopen)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:406:  - (round 1) **convergent shim finding** (V1+V2, major, blocking) — \"Package review path is test-shim only\" → **fixed** via follow-up 1 (Convex package read path wired against existing `listPackageSnapshotsForProcess` / `getPackageSnapshot` / member reads; new integration test seeded via `publishPackageSnapshot` and resolved through the real route).\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:416:- Acceptance Rationale: 3 verifier rounds, real Convex package read path now integrated end-to-end with seeded-snapshot integration test, unsupported-kind fallback integrated, cross-kind target ordering integrated, 0 real Story 1 blocking findings remain. The only remaining `blocking` verifier finding is a flaky pre-existing integration test that passes on re-run and that V1 saw as pass. Baseline up +28 with no regressions. Original \"shim\" acceptance corrected.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:432:  - `S1-F001` / `SV2-01` convergent finding — \"Package review path is test-shim only; Convex-backed production runtime cannot expose/resolve package targets\" → **accepted-risk**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:1177:  - add a minimal real websocket stack instead of more placeholder shims\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/tech-design.md:846:| Full canonical archive entry taxonomy and turn derivation | AC-3.3, AC-6.1 adjacency | Deferred to the later archive/derived-view work after Epic 6 | Later archive epic |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:63:- Full canonical archive entry taxonomy, turn derivation, or chunk/view\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/tech-design.md:681:| Full canonical archive entry taxonomy for environment/runtime events | AC-6, tech arch | Belongs to the archive follow-on slice | Feature 5 |\ntests/fixtures/ar